From 55fb05dfde2b424c15bdb31292f229a179d3a944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jackie grey <leftstick22@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:28:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add cabinet_bus plugin: socket bridge for the cabinet-bus
 server

Adds a Lua plugin (plugins/cabinet_bus/) that opens a TCP listener on
127.0.0.1:5051 and accepts newline-terminated JSON commands. The
companion Flask cabinet-bus server (in the workspace tree) drives it
via a tiny Python client (mame_client.py).

Supported commands:
  ping          - liveness probe
  get_state     - {rom, paused, frame, ...}
  pause         - emu.pause()
  resume        - emu.unpause()
  soft_reset    - manager.machine:soft_reset()
  poke_ram      - one-shot byte write to a CPU's program space
  stuck_byte    - per-frame stuck-at fault on a memory cell; the
                  plugin re-writes the cell every frame so the
                  running game cannot overwrite the fault. Mirrors
                  the BAD_RAM_CELL netlist device's fault model at
                  the MAME-CPU layer.
  clear_stuck   - disarm every armed stuck-byte fault.

The pause/resume implementation uses emu.pause()/emu.unpause()
rather than machine:pause()/machine:resume() because in MAME 0.287
the pause API is exposed on the emu module rather than on the
machine instance.

Stuck-byte faults are evaluated in the machine_frame_notifier
callback; per-frame writes use the program-space accessor on the
named CPU (defaulting to :maincpu). Centipede VRAM lives at
0x0400-0x07BF in the maincpu program space; arming a stuck-byte
there produces a visible glitch tile in the running game.

Co-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>
